# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Aicountly Lobby — React build environment template
# (repository: receptionist-aicouintly; the display name changed, the
#  identifiers did not)
#
# Copy to .env for local development:   cp .env.example .env
# .env is git-ignored and is NEVER committed or deployed.
#
# IMPORTANT — these values are read at BUILD time, not at run time.
# Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the JavaScript bundle when the app is
# built. Putting a .env on the cPanel server has NO effect on an already-built
# app: the bundle is plain static JS and never reads a file from disk. To change
# an endpoint you must rebuild and redeploy.
# (server-php is the opposite — that backend does read its own .env at runtime.
# Its template is server-php/.env.example.)
#
# Never put a secret here — anything VITE_* is public once built.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- API endpoint ----------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of this product's PHP API.
#
# Leave it EMPTY and the app calls its own origin + /api, which is exactly where
# the API workflows deploy server-php:
#
#   https://receptionist.aicountly.com/api        (production)
#   https://receptionist.gh.aicountly.com/api     (sandbox)
#
# Set it only to point somewhere else — a separate API domain, or a deployed
# sandbox API while running `npm run dev` locally. In CI the same override is
# available as the optional repository variables PROD_API_BASE_URL and
# SANDBOX_API_BASE_URL (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > Variables).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://receptionist.gh.aicountly.com/api

# --- App identity ----------------------------------------------------------
# Display name shown in the UI.
VITE_APP_NAME=Receptionist

# Deploy target this build is for: local | sandbox | production
VITE_APP_ENV=local

# --- Authentication --------------------------------------------------------
# Both of these are normally derived from the hostname and should stay unset.
# They exist for local development, where the hostname says nothing about the
# product or the environment.
#
# Portal authentication_jump product key. Derived from the hostname in the
# deployed environments (receptionist.aicountly.com and receptionist.gh.aicountly.com both
# give "receptionist").
# VITE_PRODUCT_KEY=receptionist
#
# Login portal origin. Production is https://my.aicountly.com and sandbox is
# https://sandbox.aicountly.com; localhost uses the sandbox portal.
# NOTE: this is the login redirect only. The auth API (seskey, refresh,
# validatesession) is always my.aicountly.com — see docs/auth/.
# VITE_PORTAL_LOGIN_URL=https://sandbox.aicountly.com

# --- Analytics ---------------------------------------------------------------
# GA4 (gtag) measurement ID for this product, e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX. Leave empty to
# disable analytics (no script is injected). The marketing portal reads traffic
# for this property server-side via GA4_PROPERTY_ID_SAAS_RECEPTIONIST.
VITE_GA4_SAAS_RECEPTIONIST_MEASUREMENT_ID=
#
# Generic fallback, used only if the product-specific ID above is unset.
# VITE_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# --- Aicountly Lobby ---------------------------------------------------------
# The visitor lobby: a navigable 3D reception area. See docs/lobby/.

# Path served as the public, sign-in-free visitor lobby.
#
# The lobby renders generated geometry and local demonstration journeys — no
# business data, and in the default demo mode no API call at all — so it does
# not need the portal round-trip. Every OTHER path keeps the existing SSO boot
# exactly as it was.
#
# Set this to an empty value to withdraw the public route entirely.
VITE_LOBBY_PUBLIC_PATH=/lobby

# Which service adapter answers the reception desk: demo | live
#
#   demo (default)  Journeys run entirely in the browser. Nothing is booked,
#                   nothing is sent, nobody is contacted. Every receipt is
#                   labelled as a demonstration.
#   live            Calls the application that owns each capability, and
#                   reports "unavailable" when it is not connected. It never
#                   falls back to demo data.
#
# Before switching to live, decide what an anonymous visitor on a public page is
# allowed to do — that is a product decision, not a configuration one.
VITE_LOBBY_SERVICE_MODE=demo

# Base URL of the Aicountly Appointments API.
#
# Appointments owns booking workflows and reaches Aicountly Calendar itself
# through the agreed integration. Lobby never calls Calendar directly and keeps
# no copy of an appointment or a calendar record.
#
# Leave empty until Appointments publishes a booking API contract; live mode
# reports the capability unavailable and says so, rather than guessing a path.
VITE_LOBBY_APPOINTMENTS_API_BASE_URL=

# Path on THIS product's own API that fronts the lobby reception AI,
# e.g. reception/ask — appended to VITE_API_BASE_URL.
#
# NEVER put a model key in a VITE_* variable. Vite inlines every one of them
# into the bundle at build time; they are public the moment the app is built.
# Model credentials are governed by Aicountly Console and stay server-side,
# which is why the reception AI answers through server-php rather than from the
# browser. Leave empty until that route exists.
VITE_LOBBY_RECEPTION_AI_PATH=

# Runtime manifest that replaces the procedural 3D placeholders with glTF
# models. Read at runtime, so dropping in final art is a file copy rather than a
# rebuild. A missing or malformed manifest keeps the placeholders.
# See docs/lobby/ASSETS.md.
VITE_LOBBY_ASSET_MANIFEST_URL=/lobby-assets/manifest.json
